ass=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>;</li>\n<li>PD + full inverse dynamics <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0813em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9313em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2634em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">¨</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0813em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9313em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2634em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0556em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (computed-torque feedforward).</li>\n</ol>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"feedforward\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>An arm joint tracking a swinging trajectory with PD feedback alone, with gravity feedforward, and with the full inverse model. The tracking error shrinks at each step; untick model accuracy to see what a 20 % mass error leaves.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Illustrative joint: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0962em;\">J</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span></span></span></span> kg·m², <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.47</span></span></span></span> N·m (0.5 kg at 0.3 m), <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.01</span></span></span></span> N·m·s; PD <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span> N·m/rad, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> N·m·s/rad. Reference <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.6</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span></span></span></span> rad.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Static error from gravity alone at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> rad with PD: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mord\">ℓ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.24/20</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.062</span></span></span></span> rad, 3.5°.</li>\n<li>Gravity feedforward removes that offset; what’s left comes from the inertia and friction the PD must supply as the arm swings.</li>\n<li>Inverse dynamics leaves only the error from the initial condition, which decays.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">feedforward.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nJ, mgl, b = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">9.81</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span>\nKp, Kd = <span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0</span>\nref = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> t: (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span> * np.sin(t), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span> * np.cos(t), -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span> * np.sin(t))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">run</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">mode, model_scale=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span></span>):\n    th, om = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>; errs = []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt)):\n        t = k * dt\n        r, rd, rdd = ref(t)\n        tau = Kp * (r - th) + Kd * (rd - om)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> mode <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;gravity&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;full&quot;</span>): tau += model_scale * mgl * np.sin(r)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;full&quot;</span>: tau += model_scale * J * rdd + b * rd\n        f = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> s: np.array([s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], (tau - mgl * np.sin(s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]) - b * s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) / J])\n        s = np.array([th, om])\n        k1 = f(s); k2 = f(s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k1); k3 = f(s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k2); k4 = f(s + dt * k3)\n        th, om = s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span> * (k1 + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k2 + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k3 + k4)\n        errs.append(ref(t + dt)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] - th)\n    e = np.array(errs)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.sqrt(np.mean(e[<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(e) // <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>:] ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>))      <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># RMS after the start-up transient</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_error_reduced_by_feedforward</span>():\n    e_pd, e_g, e_full = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;pd&quot;</span>), run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;gravity&quot;</span>), run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;full&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;RMS tracking error: PD <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(e_pd):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> deg, + gravity <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(e_g):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> deg, + inverse dynamics <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(e_full):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.4</span>f}</span> deg&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> e_g &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * e_pd                              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># more than 50 % reduction</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> e_full &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.01</span> * e_pd\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_model_error_still_helps</span>():\n    e_pd, e_bad = run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;pd&quot;</span>), run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;full&quot;</span>, model_scale=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.8</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;inverse dynamics with a 20 % low model: <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{np.degrees(e_bad):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> deg (<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{e_bad / e_pd:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>%}</span> of PD alone)&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> e_bad &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * e_pd\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_static_offset</span>():\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(mgl * np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>) / Kp - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0619</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span>\n\ntest_error_reduced_by_feedforward()\ntest_model_error_still_helps()\ntest_static_offset()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why use <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (the reference) rather than <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">θ</span></span></span></span> (the measurement) in the gravity feedforward?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Both work. Using the reference keeps the feedforward a pure function of the plan, free of sensor noise and outside the loop, so it can’t affect stability. Using the measurement cancels gravity exactly even when tracking is off, but puts a nonlinear term in the feedback path. Robot controllers use both, depending on noise and model quality.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A temperature loop knows the flow rate of cold water entering a tank. How would you use it?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Disturbance feedforward: compute the heat the cold flow removes, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1389em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">se</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">in</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, and add that heater power directly. The temperature controller then corrects only what the calculation gets wrong, instead of waiting for the temperature to drop.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p13-l18\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"feedback-waits-feedforward-doesn-t","title":"Feedback waits; feedforward doesn’t"},{"id":"an-arm-joint","title":"An arm joint"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p13-l18-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Gravity torque in N·m of 0.5 kg at 0.3 m, arm horizontal?</p>\n","explain":"<p>mgℓ.</p>\n","answer":1.4715,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N·m"},{"id":"p13-l18-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Static PD error in rad from that gravity at θ = 1 rad with K_p = 20?</p>\n","explain":"<p>mgℓ sin θ / K_p.</p>\n","answer":0.0619,"tol":0.01,"unit":"rad"},{"id":"p13-l18-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Inertial feedforward torque in N·m at peak reference acceleration 0.6 rad/s² with J = 0.05?</p>\n","explain":"<p>J θ̈_r.</p>\n","answer":0.03,"tol":0.001,"unit":"N·m"},{"id":"p13-l18-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Fraction of the error left if feedforward removes 90 % of the required torque (ideal linear case)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Feedback handles the remainder.</p>\n","answer":0.1,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p13-l18-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Does adding feedforward change closed-loop stability?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loop transfer function is unchanged.</p>\n","options":["no, it acts outside the loop","yes, it adds poles","it always destabilises","only for integrators"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l18-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Gravity compensation on a robot joint is an example of…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A known disturbance cancelled at the input.</p>\n","options":["disturbance feedforward","integral action","a Smith predictor","derivative filtering"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"feedforward.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nJ, mgl, b = 0.05, 0.5 * 9.81 * 0.3, 0.01\nKp, Kd = 20.0, 2.0\nref = lambda t: (1 + 0.6 * np.sin(t), 0.6 * np.cos(t), -0.6 * np.sin(t))\n\ndef run(mode, model_scale=1.0, T=20.0, dt=1e-3):\n    th, om = 1.0, 0.6; errs = []\n    for k in range(int(T / dt)):\n        t = k * dt\n        r, rd, rdd = ref(t)\n        tau = Kp * (r - th) + Kd * (rd - om)\n        if mode in (\"gravity\", \"full\"): tau += model_scale * mgl * np.sin(r)\n        if mode == \"full\": tau += model_scale * J * rdd + b * rd\n        f = lambda s: np.array([s[1], (tau - mgl * np.sin(s[0]) - b * s[1]) / J])\n        s = np.array([th, om])\n        k1 = f(s); k2 = f(s + dt / 2 * k1); k3 = f(s + dt / 2 * k2); k4 = f(s + dt * k3)\n        th, om = s + dt / 6 * (k1 + 2 * k2 + 2 * k3 + k4)\n        errs.append(ref(t + dt)[0] - th)\n    e = np.array(errs)\n    return np.sqrt(np.mean(e[len(e) // 4:] ** 2))      # RMS after the start-up transient\n\ndef test_error_reduced_by_feedforward():\n    e_pd, e_g, e_full = run(\"pd\"), run(\"gravity\"), run(\"full\")\n    print(f\"RMS tracking error: PD {np.degrees(e_pd):.2f} deg, + gravity {np.degrees(e_g):.2f} deg, + inverse dynamics {np.degrees(e_full):.4f} deg\")\n    assert e_g < 0.5 * e_pd                              # more than 50 % reduction\n    assert e_full < 0.01 * e_pd\n\ndef test_model_error_still_helps():\n    e_pd, e_bad = run(\"pd\"), run(\"full\", model_scale=0.8)\n    print(f\"inverse dynamics with a 20 % low model: {np.degrees(e_bad):.2f} deg ({e_bad / e_pd:.0%} of PD alone)\")\n    assert e_bad < 0.5 * e_pd\n\ndef test_static_offset():\n    assert abs(mgl * np.sin(1.0) / Kp - 0.0619) < 1e-3\n\ntest_error_reduced_by_feedforward()\ntest_model_error_still_helps()\ntest_static_offset()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}